#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161678 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162112 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444ad045-3c7b-5668-bc3a-e3cb49a5b6f2" :knowledge-point/title "Working With the Definition of a Conditional PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "29e739b1-8745-517f-9011-d1761364c4c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-10099" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8f5bbd64a61818dc2dd076246d9324f12d7b1123daee08f15061519a303d12d3.svg)\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the conditional probability density function $f_{Y \\,|\\, X}(y \\,|\\, x)$ and the marginal density function $f_X(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for $0 \\leq        x \\leq        1, \\: 0 \\leq        y \\leq        1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\,|\\, X}(y \\,|\\, x) =\\dfrac{f(x, y)}{f_X (x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- $f_X (x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nFrom the equation above, it follows that\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = f_{Y \\,|\\, X}(y \\,|\\, x) \\cdot f_X (x).\n$$\n\nNow, for $0 \\leq x \\leq  1, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq  1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{3{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{3{x}^{2}+1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f_{Y \\,|\\, X}(y \\,|\\, x)$ equals $0.$ As a result, the product will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the joint probability density function is the following:\n![](images/e5/e50432a004c16271fe9ffa680412a4729c9d03ce85c28d821d6b03585d2e24ba.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161679 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "3439786b-905b-5642-89d1-61b0345f79e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-10100" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n![](images/93/933179a6f35cb7362a1c1fea2c6b945796ebb8a436095552ade7b4d769690654.svg) \n\nFind $P \\left(Y <  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\,\\bigg|\\, X=1\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y \\in A \\,|\\, X = x) = \\int_A f_{Y \\,|\\, X} (y \\,|\\, x) \\, \\textrm{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $f_{Y \\,|\\, X} (y \\,|\\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function. \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}8{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =8{x}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =8{x}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}(\\sqrt{x})^{2}-0 \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for $f_X(x)$ is the following:\n\n![](images/f5/f5bc55159d59fda4918d7da4c6dd26cab5600b086e0fe00846907b901b5d467e.svg)\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\,|\\, X} (y \\,|\\, x) =\\dfrac{f(x, y)}{f_X (x)}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- $f_X (x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0<       x \\leq       1, \\: 0 \\leq       y \\leq       \\sqrt{x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{2}y}{4{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, $f_{Y \\,|\\, X} (y \\,|\\, x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n![](images/5a/5a3a34e2722798fa8b163ceb984302f300cd1d2fa6bc5fa5259e7451fceb6afc.svg)\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<\\frac{1}{2}\\,|\\,X=1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x=1)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{2y}{1}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161680 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb3b4b6a-3a24-5079-bf33-ed1c5576ffa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Conditional PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "f1c9e136-57b3-59ae-90e0-b28921be44ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-10101" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n![](images/5a/5ae264514c53b97339bfa9969057ed9462f183fc8a77658bd0615f0af148a67c.svg)\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function $f_{X \\,|\\, Y} (x \\,|\\, y)$ for $0 \\leq             x \\leq             1, \\: 0 \\leq             y \\leq  1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+xy]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+y-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2y+1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is the following:\n![](images/27/27ba59d670061d91b96f80ee5400824993311d35c9edf7a887957936d74ace8c.svg)\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_{X \\,|\\, Y} (x \\,|\\, y) = \\dfrac{f(x, y)}{f_Y (y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- $f_Y(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $0 \\leq             x \\leq             1, \\: 0 \\leq             y \\leq  1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+y}{(\\frac{2y+1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+y)}{2y+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, $f_{X \\,|\\, Y}(x \\,|\\, y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n![](images/24/242dc27ab006f389610d8f3bcd0297eed7d1809fb33b1b3b7c8b1f6b8dd532f7.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162112 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444ad045-3c7b-5668-bc3a-e3cb49a5b6f2" :knowledge-point/title "Working With the Definition of a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3915e834-8837-5560-8ead-24299d5e8d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519080} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9b3fac-024e-544d-b2ef-d778f12b1db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519109} {:answer/id #uuid "71b20e91-2ea6-54a7-a133-a83a08132141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519163} {:answer/id #uuid "745ed225-fd23-55f2-9adb-b6580902b88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519173} {:answer/id #uuid "931f0d20-f406-5676-b3e6-461c30b95ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(x+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71b20e91-2ea6-54a7-a133-a83a08132141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519163} :answer-field/id #uuid "91dddd11-2a4d-5015-8ccb-b2a5b340c5c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a8bad50-df40-5364-9a82-59b2638eab96" :question/math-academy-id "q-143607" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{X}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162112 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444ad045-3c7b-5668-bc3a-e3cb49a5b6f2" :knowledge-point/title "Working With the Definition of a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2339586b-683d-5a76-b2a4-04bd1b2acd78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519048} {:answer/id #uuid "65bb09ec-3b2d-50b3-ad37-144c0a7328e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25{x}^{2}y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519142} {:answer/id #uuid "b5172b40-2e6a-503d-a0e7-85b7d1a5c74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519291} {:answer/id #uuid "eeed90d5-0dc1-5550-b397-1136f6576d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519385} {:answer/id #uuid "f14caf42-2818-5734-9146-91625adaf049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{xy}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5172b40-2e6a-503d-a0e7-85b7d1a5c74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519291} :answer-field/id #uuid "59042651-4b23-5e23-bf65-fd2e8cfe07fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3c1aae3-e457-548d-bfd0-11222eb5ea0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-143610" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5y\\sqrt{x}, & 0<x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x\\sqrt{x}}{2}, & 0<x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{X}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0<x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0<x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5y\\sqrt{x}}{(\\frac{5x\\sqrt{x}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{x}, & 0<x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519536 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162112 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444ad045-3c7b-5668-bc3a-e3cb49a5b6f2" :knowledge-point/title "Working With the Definition of a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29233a60-9d5a-5110-abb4-845bf432054c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{e}^{-3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519058} {:answer/id #uuid "456c6b5e-5cc1-5816-9cfd-cd583482083f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}{e}^{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519100} {:answer/id #uuid "72467fb5-ec09-5cab-b876-06ab1cccd79e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x{e}^{-3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519166} {:answer/id #uuid "e7543db9-a7b9-509a-9d27-09d1c07f0fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519373} {:answer/id #uuid "f83edb0a-0c3b-51c9-afed-ceaa4bf289e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x{e}^{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72467fb5-ec09-5cab-b876-06ab1cccd79e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x{e}^{-3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519166} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52d7b68-4c65-587d-aeab-3991d8f7cc23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "403a78d0-86af-59ab-a2a0-082e022aaef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143613" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-3y}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{X}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nFrom the equation above, it follows that\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\cdot {f}_{X}(x).\n$$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 0,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =3{e}^{-3y}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =6x{e}^{-3y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ equals $0.$ As a result, the product will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the joint probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6x{e}^{-3y}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519563 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e7d0ba3-02f6-59a7-be65-bf8f3801013a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519040} {:answer/id #uuid "3da4eaa1-6cda-5d99-b813-20a4d9738e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519091} {:answer/id #uuid "58bb21c1-450d-505d-b6dc-9db3c242bf5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519125} {:answer/id #uuid "70730109-0401-592f-81a2-e4405b7b0f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519162} {:answer/id #uuid "e7050eac-3947-55c2-b302-d2bd01b29003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e7d0ba3-02f6-59a7-be65-bf8f3801013a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519040} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c446274-85cc-56ab-805a-72556fc77fd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91a2a3a1-8ae1-5b13-976f-9bc558602e26" :question/math-academy-id "q-143619" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3x, & \\,y<x<1\\,,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{6}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$  \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{y}^{1}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{y}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(1-{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}(1-{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $y<x<1\\,,\\,0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{(\\frac{3}{2}(1-{y}^{2}))} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{1-{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{1-{y}^{2}}, & \\,0<y<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{4}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{6}) & =P(\\frac{1}{4}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{1}{6})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1}\\frac{2x}{(1-{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2})}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1}\\frac{2x}{(\\frac{35}{36})}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{35}{\\int }_{1/4}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{35}{[{x}^{2}]}_{1/4}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{35}(1-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30be591d-18e4-56ca-bd11-2cb0e73aa66b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519068} {:answer/id #uuid "52c36d35-dfd3-59ca-b51c-6f8f7df4b4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519119} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccaa219-a0ea-583d-9e0c-efdebeabb3e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519220} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f9475b-b7d3-5932-90b4-6269e7ee9da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519255} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b6de00-aaa3-58b8-919b-6ae993100929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0f9475b-b7d3-5932-90b4-6269e7ee9da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519255} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7448890-beaa-51f5-b2f0-83828889fb49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a05be7fd-94f3-5604-ad03-bc6e74737579" :question/math-academy-id "q-143620" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{5}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{4}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{5}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{4}{3}) & ={\\int }_{1/5}^{1}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{4}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/5}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}]_{1/5}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28a6421c-8bb1-5e74-b5ce-4488dab6060e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519057} {:answer/id #uuid "93edd067-6d4d-5723-af3e-e6c5a01044b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519238} {:answer/id #uuid "a929b9b7-76e2-511c-af43-a8af03c8efa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519271} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f0f68c-757f-5ea6-b804-da070251f3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519296} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc4d93c-b651-5691-9445-a738e7a4241d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbc4d93c-b651-5691-9445-a738e7a4241d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519300} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2ec7e2d-e700-5713-ba66-48bf13c5d6e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d2c3b01f-8b1d-5c9b-95df-4bf4aec9fac1" :question/math-academy-id "q-143622" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}y\\sqrt{x}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3}{4}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{x}{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{x}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0<x<1,0<y<2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{4}y\\sqrt{x})}{(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}y, & \\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{4}<Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{4}) & =P(\\frac{1}{4}<Y<\\frac{3}{4}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{3/4}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x=\\frac{3}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{3/4}\\frac{1}{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{1/4}^{3/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c35ea81-1fba-5743-bc51-d55ebe9293ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411702} {:answer/id #uuid "4668fa6c-efd9-5349-af00-60d3491fb89f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411715} {:answer/id #uuid "4822c638-df09-5a29-b181-ed51e650cdfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411716} {:answer/id #uuid "debe288e-f7cd-5ceb-8f13-e4258cc3d96c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411803} {:answer/id #uuid "e02c333f-cc9c-5916-848d-431524aca433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4668fa6c-efd9-5349-af00-60d3491fb89f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411715} :answer-field/id #uuid "a596b6c7-9c32-5ca9-bbc7-7ea06ecbb649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd343afe-c54e-593d-8dc2-ed57fc5e3a91" :question/math-academy-id "q-143625" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =P(X<\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb3b4b6a-3a24-5079-bf33-ed1c5576ffa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f62924-6dd5-52ac-bd28-479c20aca94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519045} {:answer/id #uuid "75fd5efd-a360-53f9-9006-6a6a1d8e159f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9{y}^{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519176} {:answer/id #uuid "849cc2b5-4f4e-50d8-9169-5a909d23bf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519201} {:answer/id #uuid "d03e8f09-0450-5bd4-8ebb-657acd93cbc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519331} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3bcf1a-3dc4-5e1f-8c31-d1add2e63f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849cc2b5-4f4e-50d8-9169-5a909d23bf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519201} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ea5fec5-a0af-570b-bb41-e2eb4069b829" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f873ff79-08e6-53a2-8403-85dc4a081919" :question/math-academy-id "q-143633" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{14}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{14}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{14}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{14}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{14}\\cdot [27-(-1)] \\\\  & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{14})}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{28}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb3b4b6a-3a24-5079-bf33-ed1c5576ffa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0949f974-6ec9-5ea8-8abf-e774af8d8181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519006} {:answer/id #uuid "492c26d0-4de7-559c-b3c6-23e5c24bcbeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{y}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519108} {:answer/id #uuid "a324c1a2-ed56-5a2e-94f6-eaae1cefbad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519261} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a0eac0-1e8a-5d29-8b9c-eb8fd34e5908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x+y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519336} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3319c5-cf98-59ef-a3ca-016ee01f17e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{x+y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0949f974-6ec9-5ea8-8abf-e774af8d8181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519006} :answer-field/id #uuid "12430dc2-f5be-5736-9417-2b04f094d03d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1967c2eb-a9e1-5379-9ffd-3708e127b5c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-143637" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x+y}}{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{{e}^{x+y}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}\\cdot {e}^{y}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{e}^{x+y}}{2})}{(\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2})} \\\\  & ={e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y}, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb3b4b6a-3a24-5079-bf33-ed1c5576ffa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41d76f20-9c01-572e-9bec-b4534a624512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16xy(4-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519095} {:answer/id #uuid "697349f9-9995-58d2-a52b-dd64ff7d8349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{y}^{2}(4-y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519146} {:answer/id #uuid "9307b7d8-60d8-57f7-a4d6-b9b56f00ed28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}(4-y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519235} {:answer/id #uuid "b28cbfc4-beef-5aec-838d-bb8099b27e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8x}{y(4-y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519285} {:answer/id #uuid "bd07ced2-884b-510d-b5ef-173e5b1d1caf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4xy}{4-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b28cbfc4-beef-5aec-838d-bb8099b27e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8x}{y(4-y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519285} :answer-field/id #uuid "f41b096e-82c3-5dae-bf25-98903c7a8157" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b02f20a-35d0-57b1-ada9-f1273f1f3904" :question/math-academy-id "q-143641" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x{y}^{2}}{32} & \\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0<y<4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{y}}\\frac{5x{y}^{2}}{32}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{32}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{y}}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{32}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{64}\\cdot (y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{y}^{3}(4-y)}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{y}^{3}(4-y)}{256}, & \\,0<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0<y<4,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{5x{y}^{2}}{32})}{(\\frac{5{y}^{3}(4-y)}{256})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8x}{y(4-y)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x}{y(4-y)}, & \\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0<y<4, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162112 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444ad045-3c7b-5668-bc3a-e3cb49a5b6f2" :knowledge-point/title "Working With the Definition of a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0892c552-097f-5f93-9810-e84e7169c037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519004} {:answer/id #uuid "523d9b76-cebc-5f99-9fbb-0e7e6db546ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519118} {:answer/id #uuid "54b15bb6-9e55-5f2e-9988-527ed5cf6ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519122} {:answer/id #uuid "653110f4-0f51-5e63-bd19-c507464feb61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{9x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519140} {:answer/id #uuid "726600a2-7334-5b46-8aea-ffaea3283afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "523d9b76-cebc-5f99-9fbb-0e7e6db546ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe76e9c1-efee-513d-8f78-b81b7c1d3e0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6d9b032-eda8-55d5-b69c-37b94f5fdf98" :question/math-academy-id "q-144941" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{10}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+9}{10}, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{X}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{10})}{(\\frac{3{x}^{2}+9}{10})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}+9}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162112 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444ad045-3c7b-5668-bc3a-e3cb49a5b6f2" :knowledge-point/title "Working With the Definition of a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e8af9d3-e625-57a2-9753-9a16f2c5bfd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{3y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519158} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c0f0ef-519d-5451-a179-30787df74d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519264} {:answer/id #uuid "bed11b29-67d4-5909-9036-4139a697822e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+y}{3y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519305} {:answer/id #uuid "d1fe2e08-4582-5e78-9887-77cb0f66a621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+y}{y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519335} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5bfc28-404f-5301-a9fb-f28a54d7b0fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+y}{y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e8af9d3-e625-57a2-9753-9a16f2c5bfd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{3y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519158} :answer-field/id #uuid "83d69883-60e5-51a8-8587-9ac2f3c97229" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fde66fe1-1f42-5587-ae07-4dc1d6de7d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-144943" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3y+1}{8}, & 0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{8})}{(\\frac{3y+1}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{3y+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{3y+1}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb3b4b6a-3a24-5079-bf33-ed1c5576ffa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab5ae73e-ff79-5c66-9c67-13be3d4cfbbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x+y}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519274} {:answer/id #uuid "b91672bb-93d2-50b7-8eb9-de13911fe838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y+1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519294} {:answer/id #uuid "c97c539f-b49d-5a10-804a-fdc7d978fe94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{4x+y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519320} {:answer/id #uuid "de6ccd7b-feeb-5a8f-8280-45a2401779e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+y}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519358} {:answer/id #uuid "e0409b5a-bd0f-5146-b9ba-ff2fcb1d149b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+y}{2(2x+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0409b5a-bd0f-5146-b9ba-ff2fcb1d149b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+y}{2(2x+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519363} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e16ecfd-ecda-506a-a72f-57bf0aaac1ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0309d911-015b-5e4c-9346-30c2d14fb0b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-145100" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{4}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2x+y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {[2xy+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot [4x+2] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2x+y}{4})}{(\\frac{2x+1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+y}{4x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{2(2x+1)}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb3b4b6a-3a24-5079-bf33-ed1c5576ffa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b5b39e-b50f-5667-85aa-10f98316c5ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+y}{3(y+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518997} {:answer/id #uuid "099b70eb-adf5-5c0b-935e-950c1e096556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{2y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519007} {:answer/id #uuid "41e1bf01-9793-54f8-9d28-af6f78aec84b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y+2}{x+2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519096} {:answer/id #uuid "476db03a-613d-54d1-8c90-950c1e79d5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y+1}{2({x}^{2}+y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519104} {:answer/id #uuid "5dfec5ee-76b0-5274-a7c7-3fbca567739b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{3(2y+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dfec5ee-76b0-5274-a7c7-3fbca567739b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{3(2y+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519133} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb8d45a-30b0-5de1-a6e8-4ab5704badae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60bd267c-251c-5e47-b502-67f097fb7ef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-145101" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{12}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{y}{6})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{36}+\\frac{xy}{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{36}+\\frac{3y}{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{y}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y+3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y+3}{4}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{12})}{(\\frac{2y+3}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{3(2y+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{3(2y+3)}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ea33cc-5f23-589d-8c23-7c092cbc2f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519019} {:answer/id #uuid "2589e333-131b-51b5-ad48-bd1130f65246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519052} {:answer/id #uuid "871f5b77-fc09-5ab2-85ec-496ea72f30af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519207} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccd639c-35b2-5792-9629-fe551a25b276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519221} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b2770a-9e7a-586b-b171-0fbdfcac8124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2589e333-131b-51b5-ad48-bd1130f65246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519052} :answer-field/id #uuid "6064d30a-0a9e-55a1-8d02-c3cb038cef8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "05787bc3-261f-5b82-bb66-810cc0eb28ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-145108" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y+x}{4y+2}, & \\,0<x<2,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{3}{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{3}{4}) & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{y}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{3}{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{3/4}\\frac{(2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+x)}{(4\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{1/4}^{3/4}(x+\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{3x}{2}]}_{1/4}^{3/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[{x}^{2}+3x]_{1/4}^{3/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}({(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+3(\\frac{3}{4})-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}-3(\\frac{1}{4})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\frac{9}{16}+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
